  "id": "COMPOUND:30039 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a direct relationship between 2,2,4-Trimethyl-3-cyclohexenecarboxaldehyde and the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, mediated through the compound ME-180 and its derivatives. All three pathways indicate that the target compound acts as a ligand or modulator of ME-180, which in turn targets the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. This suggests a potential mechanism where the target compound influences the activity of ME-180, which then interacts with the polycomb group (PcG) complex, a key regulator of gene expression. The shared target of ME-180 across different pathways implies a common functional role, possibly in epigenetic regulation. The evidence is consistent and supports a unified mechanism, though the exact nature of the interaction between the target compound and ME-180 remains to be elucidated.",
